## Dispositions of the r1 findings

- F1 fixed. The aspect and short-side rule now covers every loaded photo whose src holds
  `/images/products/`, every photo with a `program-card` or `product-block` ancestor, and
  `/images/blended-learning.png` through an explicit list. The Tutor picture and the
  report-results picture are inside the rule. A guard pushes a problem when the list is empty,
  so the rule cannot pass on a missing deliverable. spec.md records the wider scope.
- F2 fixed. An `img` in a page `main` with an empty src adds a problem instead of being skipped.
  All six pages in the set have a `main` element. The badge skip needs both signals: a file name
  that starts with `qr`, `logo`, or `icon`, and an alt that names a logo, an icon, or a QR code.
  A photo named `icon-guide.png` now counts. `line-qr.jpg` also counts, which matches the
  two-signal rule, and Red r3 records it as loaded, visible, and uncovered at 100 x 100.
- F3 fixed. Plan task 1.1 now says the pre-fix e2e run was skipped and that the hero unit test at
  `8193625ca^` is the pre-fix proof. The stale claim is gone.

## F4, the PM text overlap limit of 10 percent

The rule measures the union of the clipped text boxes with coordinate compression over the
visible photo area, the same denominator as the cover test. I checked the two fooling vectors.

- An ancestor that holds the photo is skipped. An ancestor's own text nodes sit in normal flow
  and cannot paint over an in-flow child image without contrived float or negative-margin CSS.
  spec.md AC-1 documents the skip as a rule. A positioned text element inside the ancestor does
  not hold the image, so it is counted.
- A `figcaption` is skipped only when its top starts at or below the photo bottom. In that case
  it cannot intersect the photo, and the generic clip test would drop it anyway. A caption that
  overlaps the photo is counted.

The rule runs on the counted set, the same set as the cover test. That matches the thumbnail
rule in spec.md AC-1. One proof gap stays, recorded as F5.

## Home Mastery card

Below `lg` the card is centered under the photo with `mx-auto w-3/4 max-w-sm`. From `lg` the
corner placement stays. The e2e assertion runs for `/` at 390 px in both locales. It fails when
there is no figure, when the hero photo does not count, or when the card is neither within
10 percent of the viewport centre nor 90 percent of the photo width. The home page renders
exactly one figure, so `figure.first()` targets the Mastery card. Red r3 proved the assertion
first: at `d43334ba6` it failed `home en 390 px` and `home th 390 px` with the card 23 percent
from the centre and 40 percent of the photo width.

## Findings

- F5 (medium, nonblocking). The 10 percent text rule has no failing-first proof and no recorded
  nonzero measurement. The Red r3 raw log holds 12 report lines, all `textOverlap=0%`, and zero
  `textBoxes=` labels. The Red r3 run failed only the Mastery card assertion, so no case ever
  drove the union past zero. A natural fixture existed at `40419d4bc`, where the report-results
  text box covered `blended-learning.png` 100 percent, and it was not run. Static reading finds
  the union algorithm correct, so the finding stays nonblocking. Cheap proof: run the new spec
  against a build of `40419d4bc` and confirm the text rule fails that case.
- D1 (accepted, carried from r1). The report-results card stays stacked at every width, because
  the grid cell is one third wide at `lg` and the stacked card keeps text off the photo.

